# Copy to .env. Never commit .env — it is gitignored.
#
# Every credential here is optional. Signal boots without any of them and
# tells you which capabilities are dark:
#
#     pnpm signal status
#
# Hacker News and RSS ingestion need nothing at all, so you can run the whole
# pipeline end to end before setting any of this up.

# ─── Models ───
# Which provider is used is set in signal.config.ts under `llm`, not here.
# This file only carries the credential, if the provider needs one.
#
# A local OpenAI-compatible runtime (llama-server, vLLM, LM Studio, Ollama)
# usually needs no key at all — leave both of these unset and it will work.
# Check with: pnpm signal llm check
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# LLM_API_KEY=

# ─── Reddit ─── Register a "script" type app at https://www.reddit.com/prefs/apps
# The client id is the string under the app name; the secret is labelled
# "secret". Also set http.userAgent in signal.config.ts to your real username —
# Reddit throttles generic agents hard.
#
# Client id and secret alone are enough to READ. Username and password are only
# needed to POST, which never happens without you clicking approve.
#
# One identity per platform. There is no second account, by design.
# REDDIT_CLIENT_ID=
# REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET=
# REDDIT_USERNAME=
# REDDIT_PASSWORD=

# ─── Stripe ─── Phase 4: conversion attribution.
# The webhook secret is what makes an incoming payload trustworthy. Without it
# the webhook receiver rejects everything, which is the correct default.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ─── Firebase edge ─── Phase 4: pulling clicks and conversions back down.
# Project: signal-edge-aionx
# SIGNAL_EDGE_PROJECT_ID=signal-edge-aionx
# SIGNAL_EDGE_PULL_TOKEN=

# Passphrase for the encrypted SQLite backup. Minimum 16 characters.
# Lose this and the backups are unreadable — put it in your password manager.
# SIGNAL_BACKUP_PASSPHRASE=

# ─── Local overrides ───
# Point at another database file, e.g. for a scratch run.
# SIGNAL_DATABASE_URL=file:./data/scratch.db

# Set to 1 to make every outbound request fail instead of hitting a real API.
# SIGNAL_OFFLINE=0
